cope\": \"Crossref bibliographic metadata and abstracts where supplied; not full papers\", \"excerpt\": \"[{\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.56975/ijrar.v12i3.317361\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"Does Consciousness Emerge from Information Integration in Mind and Machines?\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.56975/ijrar.v12i3.317361\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2025]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.1007/978-981-96-6170-1_20\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"How Does Information Emerge from a Black Hole?\\\"], \\\"URL\\\": \\\"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-981-96-6170-1_20\\\", \\\"published\\\": {\\\"date-parts\\\": [[2025]]}}, {\\\"DOI\\\": \\\"10.2139/ssrn.6310458\\\", \\\"title\\\": [\\\"How Does Durable Coordinated Power Emerge?\\\"], \\\"abstract\\\": \\\"<jats:p>How does durable coordinated power emerge? The question is constitutive: not how power is distributed or legitimised, but what conditions make it structurally possible. From three minimal conditions-plurality, interdependence, and processing (interpretation, evaluation, anticipation)-this paper derives a structural chain showing that every path to coordination passes through meaning, and every path to durable coordinated power passes through a seven-dimensional coordination architecture. Four theorems specify its structural properties: it constitutes a functionally autonomous domain, it is critical infrastructure, it requires multimodal coherence, and structural advantage requires dimensional completeness. Six cases-Augustan Rome, Afghanistan, the 2024 United States presidential election, Germany, the European Union, and NATO-apply the derivation to historic and contemporary coordination structures, identifying conditions of stability and failure at a functional systemic level across all seven dimensions. Two independent derivation paths-bottom-up from the three starting conditions, top-down from five canonical premises-converge on these results. The derivation specifies conditions under which each element obtains 